/* MEASURED IN THE LIVE PAGE rather than copied from the slider next door, and the
   copy would have been wrong. The stepper is `ha-control-number-buttons` inside
   `hui-numeric-input-card-feature` -- note "card", not "tile". HA renamed that element,
   so the volume tile's `hui-numeric-input-tile-feature` selector matches nothing; its
   slider is ember only because --control-slider-color INHERITS down from ha-card.
   Confirmed live: --em-bed resolves to #4A1002 and --control-slider-color to #E05A08
   on that card, with zero elements matching the third selector.

   THE STEPPER IS LEFT DELIBERATELY NATIVE, for two reasons.
   1. It cannot be recoloured from here. It declares
      --control-number-buttons-background-color on its OWN :host (falling back to
      --disabled-color), so a value inherited from ha-card loses the cascade. Reaching
      it needs a four-level shadow-DOM chain -- the same kind of chain HA has already
      invalidated once above, and it fails silently when it goes stale.
   2. It should not be. The slider's gold is a FILL encoding 65%; a stepper has no
      fill, so gilding eight discrete stops would imply a level they do not carry.
   Ember identity is carried here by the card border and by the lit stop in the ladder
   below -- both verified rendering. */
ha-card { border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--em-glow) 45%, transparent);
  border-radius:12px;
  background:linear-gradient(100deg,
    color-mix(in srgb, var(--em-bed) 22%, var(--card-background-color)) 0%,
    var(--card-background-color) 55%);
  box-shadow:0 0 22px color-mix(in srgb, var(--em-coal) 28%, transparent); }

